name "sec:Related-Work"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the related work section,
 you write down what is actually know in the context of your work,
 i.e.
 evidence that exists in the context of your work.
 The goal is not to make any statements whether or not someone believes something is good or not.
 This sections contains evidence.
 This also implies that your personal opinion does not play any role in this section.
 
\series bold
Again,
 do not state something just because some other author stated it – if you make a statement here,
 give the corresponding evidence.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It is hard to estimate how many pages this chapter has,
 but in case it is less than 3 pages,
 you probably have not intensively searched for studies that are relevant for you present study.
\end_layout

