\begin_layout Standard
There is this other subchapter that play a role.
 In this chapter,
 you should mention those experiments that influenced your experimental design.
 Reasons that you mention those experiments are for example,
 that a certain measurements is used that you used as well or something else from the experimental design that is necessary for your work.
 For example,
 just the decision that you use time to completion (i.e.
 you let subject do a task until the task has been fulfilled).
 Note,
 that it is not necessary to write down such experiments in detail – you just need to mention the experiments and those parts from the experiment that are relevant for you.
 I.e.
 this subchapter typically does not require p-values or something.
\end_layout

