\begin_layout Standard
While researching and developing code snippets for an initial experiment on the readability of nested if-statements,
 it became apparent that the way indentation length affects reading time was not as straightforward as commonly assumed.
 This observation motivated the investigation of indentation as a central topic of this thesis.
 This experiment presents the initial,
 most basic setup used to study this relationship:
 nested if-statements with a single-word condition per level,
 compared across four fixed indentation lengths.
\end_layout

