\begin_layout Standard
We want to design a controlled experiment where the participant receives code snippets of nested if-statements,
 in order to measure the effect of different indentation lengths and nesting levels.
 To compare the different lengths and levels,
 we want to measure the reading time for each code snippet.
 For this purpose,
 we measure the reaction time,
 i.e.,
 the time it takes for the participant to complete the task,
 which serves as an approximation for the reading time.
