\begin_layout Standard
Each JavaScript code snippet consists of a chain of nine nested if-statements,
 generated recursively so that each if-statement's then-branch is either the next nested if-statement or,
 at the innermost level,
 a return value of 0.
 Each if-statement's else-branch returns a distinct integer between 1 and 10,
 these ten values then are randomly shuffled and assigned across the nine nesting levels,
 ensuring that the correct answer cannot be assigned from the position of the highlighted condition alone.
 Each nested if-statement is printed on its own line,
 indented by a fixed number of spaces equal to the product of the indentation length treatment and the nesting depth.
 The condition corresponding to the treatment's Level is highlighted with a red background,
 indicating that this if-statement,
 and all deeper nested if-statements,
 evaluate to false,
 so that the associated else-branch's return value is the correct answer.
