Unlike the preliminary experiments,
 in which the author was the sole,
 well-practiced participant,
 this experiment required participants to both locate the closing bracket and read and enter the correct number,
 adding a motor component to the measured reaction time.
 Since participants differ in typing proficiency and familiarity with the keyboard layout used,
 part of the measured reaction time and part of the variance attributed to Subject may reflect differences in response execution rather than differences in reading or comprehension time.
 Additionally,
